  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
      XSD 1.0 schema definition for D365FO EDT metadata (AxEdt).
      This schema is intended for validators with XML Schema 1.0 support,
      such as the .NET XmlSchemaSet validator.
      The root element is abstract to enforce xsi:type usage in XSD 1.0 workflows.
      Based on metrics captured from D365ApplicationExtended.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <xs:include schemaLocation="AxEdt.SharedTypes.xsd"/>

  <xs:complexType name="AxEdtCollectionType">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
      XSD 1.0 note: each EDT xsi:type is declared as a standalone complex type.
      The content model for each type is duplicated on purpose so that every
      type lists only the elements observed for that type while still allowing
      those elements in any order via xs:all.
      The abstract AxEdt element is typed as xs:anyType so xsi:type can bind to
      these standalone concrete types without forcing inheritance.
      
      Shared by all EDT types: Name, DisplayLength, Extends, Label,
      ConfigurationKey, CountryRegionCodes, HelpText, ArrayElements,
      Relations, TableReferences, ReferenceTable, IsObsolete.
      
      Shared by a subset of EDT types: Alignment, AllowNegative,
      ButtonImage, CollectionLabel, ControlClass, DateDay, DateMonth,
      DateSeparator, DateYear, Direction, DisplaceNegative,
      DisplayHeight, EnforceHierarchy, FormHelp, MaxDateLabel,
      PresenceClass, PresenceIndicatorAllowed, PresenceMethod,
      RotateSign, ShowZero, SignDisplay, Tags, TimeHours, TimeMinute,
      TimeSeconds.
      
      Used by a single EDT type only: Adjustment, AutoInsSeparator,
      ChangeCase, DatabaseStringSize, DataInteractorFactory, DateFormat,
      DecimalSeparator, EnumType, FormatMST, NoOfDecimals,
      NoOfDecimalsIsExtensible, Scale, StringSize,
      StringSizeIsExtensible, Style, ThousandSeparator, TimeFormat,
      TimeSeparator, TimezonePreference.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

